Voyager 3.5.2 documentation
==========================

This drawer is the Workbench documentation for the amigazen project
release of Voyager 3.5.2 (classic 68k).

The original VaporWare V3 "complete documentation" archive was
distributed from http://v3.vapor.com/ (Oliver Wagner, 2000). That
site is offline. Historical notes remain at:

  https://zapek.com/software/voyager/

Source, changelog, licence, and the full feature list for 3.5.2 are
in the GitHub tree and on the amigazen project site:

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager
  http://www.amigazen.com/voyager/
  voyager@amigazen.com

Files in this drawer
--------------------

  Readme.Docs     This file.
  voyager3docs/   VaporWare HTML manual (open main.html). Factory
                  fastlink "Docs" loads this from PROGDIR: (it
                  replaces the old www.vapor.com favourite).
  ReadMe.mui      MUI (MagicUserInterface) copyright and registration
                  notes from Stefan Stuntz. Voyager still requires MUI.
  ReadMe.TearOff  TearOff MUI classes by Szymon Ulatowski.

In the 3.5.2 Workbench tree
---------------------------

  V               The browser (SAS/C 68k).
  V.ReadMe        Program readme for 3.5.2. History for 3.4, 3.3, and
                  3.2 and older is in CHANGELOG.md in the source tree.
  Libs/           MUI classes used by Voyager.
  Plugins/        Including voyager_ssl.vlib (AmiTLS / TLS 1.2, SNI).
  Certificates/   CA bundle (cacert.pem) required for HTTPS.
  Buttons/        Toolbar imagery.
  Cache/          Disk cache (created/used at run time).

A TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library) must be running. AmiTLS
(LIBS:amitls.library) is required for HTTPS. cybergraphics.library
is used when present for RTG. 

HTML manual (voyager3docs)
--------------------------

The missing V3 HTML documentation is in voyager3docs/. Start at
main.html. From a factory-reset prefs set, click the Docs fastlink
(file:///PROGDIR:Docs/voyager3docs/main.html).

Voyager.guide was a separate AmigaGuide from the VaporWare pack.
Use the HTML manual, README.md / CHANGELOG.md from the source
release, or the URLs above.

Limited 3.3 line (after 3.2)
----------------------------

Voyager 3.2 (16.4.2000) was the last boxed public product. A limited
3.3 alpha / public-beta line followed (from August 2000): new layout
engine and window framework, vertical navigation panel, optional
TearOff, CManager aliases in the URL gadget, ftp. auto-prefix, HTML
error pages for HTTP 4xx/5xx, AS225 removed. Public betas 3.3.65 and
3.3.75; 3.3.126 (27.12.2002) for 68k and MorphOS, not to be installed
over 3.2. Printing and some layout/JS gaps remained. A short 3.4 CVS
series followed. Headline list: CHANGELOG.md. Per-build 3.3.0-3.3.127
log: Source/V.ReadMe in the GitHub tree.

